    "result": "Excellent! The fix is working correctly. Here's what I did:\n\n## Summary\n\n**The Problem**: The `--ci` flag was being consumed by the main `frai` CLI before the `gate` subcommand received it, preventing the GitHub Actions workflow from being created.\n\n**The Solution**: I made two changes to `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`:\n\n1. Added `.enablePositionalOptions()` to the main program (line 603) to allow subcommands to use pass-through options\n2. Added `.passThroughOptions()` to the gate command (line 741) to prevent the parent command from consuming options meant for the subcommand\n\n**Verification**: \n- Rebuilt the package with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n- Tested `frai gate init --ci` and confirmed both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` are now created successfully\n\nThe `--ci` flag is now properly passed through to the `frai-gate` CLI, which handles creating the workflow file as expected.",
